#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:14
msgid ""
"This function downloads the dataset from the GMT data server, caches it in a "
"user data directory (usually ``~/.gmt/server/earth/earth_faa/`` or ``~/.gmt/"
"server/earth/earth_faaerror/``), and load the dataset as an :class:`xarray."
"DataArray`. An internet connection is required the first time around, but "
"subsequent calls will load the dataset from the local data directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:20
msgid ""
"The dataset can also be accessed by specifying a file name in any grid "
"processing function or plotting method, using the following file name "
"format: **@**\\ *earth_faa_type*\\_\\ *res*\\_\\ *reg*. *earth_faa_type* is "
"the GMT name for the dataset. The available options are **earth_faa** and "
"**earth_faaerror**. *res* is the grid resolution; *reg* is the grid "
"registration type (**p** for pixel registration, **g** for gridline "
"registration). If *reg* is omitted (e.g., ``@earth_faa_01d``), the gridline-"
"registered grid will be loaded for grid processing functions and the pixel-"
"registered grid will be loaded for plotting functions. If *res* is also "
"omitted (i.e., ``@earth_faa``), GMT automatically selects a suitable "
"resolution based on the current region and projection settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:31
msgid ""
"This dataset comes with two color palette table (CPT) files, ``@earth_faa."
"cpt`` and ``@earth_faaerror.cpt``. To use the dataset-specific CPT when "
"plotting the dataset, explicitly set ``cmap=\"@earth_faa.cpt\"`` or "
"``cmap=\"@earth_faaerror.cpt\"``, otherwise GMT's default CPT (*google/"
"turbo*) will be used. If the dataset is referenced by the file name in a "
"grid plotting method, the dataset-specific CPT file is used automatically "
"unless another CPT is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:38
msgid ""
"Refer to :gmt-datasets:`earth-faa.html` and :gmt-datasets:`earth-faaerror."
"html` for more details about available datasets, including version "
"information and references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "參數"

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:42
msgid ""
"The grid resolution. The suffix ``d`` and ``m`` stand for arc-degrees and "
"arc-minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:45
msgid ""
"The subregion of the grid to load, in the form of a sequence [*xmin*, "
"*xmax*, *ymin*, *ymax*] or an ISO country code. Required for grids with "
"resolutions higher than 5 arc-minutes (i.e., ``\"05m\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:49
msgid ""
"Grid registration type. Either ``\"pixel\"`` for pixel registration or "
"``\"gridline\"`` for gridline registration. Default is ``None``, which means "
"``\"gridline\"`` for all resolutions except ``\"01m\"`` which is "
"``\"pixel\"`` only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_free_air_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_free_air_anomaly.load_earth_free_air_anomaly:54
msgid ""
"By default, the Earth free-air anomaly values are returned. Set to ``True`` "
"to return the related uncertainties instead."
msgstr ""

